{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789757610,"nonce":"JPqmCMJznG8Zr12AXyvebRRTDTk=","title":"The plugins on caribou's shared ABI","message":"Under caribou, native access for every hosted language is caribou's\nplugin ABI (caribou_abi, caribou issue\n3211ae57e305c07df06500c7592cce5f21abe9d365c29c089775df5f24ea0e3d):\na cdylib whose `plugin!` header lists typed `extern \"C\"` items\n(scalars, `Text`, `Value`, class objects by `\u0026T`/`Box\u003cT\u003e`), loaded by\nthe driver from `plugins/` or a bundle's NativeLib sections, and\npublished as a language of its own that Wren imports as\n`import \"sqlite:Connection\" for Connection` and Haxe as\n`import sqlite.Connection`. The plugin reaches the core through a\nhost table: strings, kept values (`Kept`), `host::call`, `raise`.\n\nThe plugins under plugins/ (sqlite, window, gpu, image, audio, noise,\nparticles, physics, hello) are on wlift_abi: slot-shaped entry points\n`fn(vm: *mut WrenVm)` reading `slot(vm, i)` and writing `set_return`,\nwith lists, maps and typed arrays through `wlift_plugin_*` symbols the\nhost exports, reached by `import \"@hatch:sqlite\"`. Wren only.\n\nWhat has to be decided before the work:\n\n1. One ABI or two. A plugin on caribou's ABI is a set of typed\n   functions; the same crate can also keep its wlift_abi entry points\n   behind a feature so standalone wlift keeps loading it, at the cost\n   of two surfaces per plugin. Or wlift's loader (runtime::foreign)\n   learns caribou_abi's tables and calls typed functions itself, and\n   the wlift_abi surface retires. caribou_abi is a dependency-free\n   header crate, but it is caribou's, and the rule is that runtimes\n   do not depend on caribou; whether that rule covers the ABI crate is\n   the owner's call.\n\n2. Collections. The typed ABI has no list, map or typed array. Either\n   caribou's host table grows `len`/`index`/`set_index`/`invoke` over\n   `Value` (a plugin then handles any language's list through the\n   bridge, which is the right shape for \"every language\") and typed\n   arrays cross as a plugin class with a byte view, or these plugins\n   keep taking `Value`s and reading them through wlift_abi, which is\n   Wren-only again.\n\n3. Order. `hello` and `noise` first (scalars and strings, nothing\n   kept), then `sqlite` (objects: Connection, Statement; rows as\n   lists need item 2), then the windowing/GPU set, which also carry\n   event callbacks (`Kept` + `host::call`) and the frame pump.\n\nNot started. Nothing here changes until the owner picks 1 and 2.","files":null}]}